---
title: "Node.js SDK"
description: "Use @veristamp/nqql for native QQL parsing, policy injection, planning, and Qdrant execution."
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

{% terminal title="Install" %}
npm install @veristamp/nqql
{% /terminal %}

{% qqlExample title="Input used below" %}
QUERY TEXT 'incident response' FROM runbooks
USING dense
LIMIT 5;
{% /qqlExample %}

```javascript
const { Client, parse, isValid } = require("@veristamp/nqql");

if (!isValid(query)) throw new Error("invalid QQL");

const client = new Client({ url: "http://localhost:6333" });
const report = await client.execute(query);
console.log(report.ok, report.results);
```

## Parse and isolate

```javascript
const [stmt] = parse(query);
stmt.injectFilter("tenant_id", "=", "acme");
stmt.shardKey = "acme";
await client.execute(stmt);
```

`parse` wraps the native full-script parser and always returns an array of
statement handles. `parseJson` is the raw JSON forwarding form.

{% aside type="note" title="Platform packages" %}
The package loads the matching N-API binary for supported Linux, macOS, and
Windows targets. Node.js 18 or newer is required.
{% /aside %}
